 "findings": [
  "Each binding() rehashes 807 files in ~1.86 s; the two detector model directories take ~1.67 s of it (1.31 GB). The execute path calls it 5 times per cycle: TaskManager.execute once and ExecutionService.submit for every segment, so segment 1 waits for two of them.",
  "Each segment start (cycle state entry to controller acceptance) takes ~1.9 s, almost all of it that rehash inside the 20 ms supervisor tick; during it the Cycle supervisor does not tick (the execution process keeps supervising the motion). Rule-required waits are separate: 0.4 s arrival dwell, 1 s pressure dwell plus the wait for the first qualifying heartbeat.",
  "Child-side submit: trajectory-package.json serialization 0.04-0.06 s; pipe transfer ~5 ms; everything else < 3 ms on fake IO (the real controller payload TCP query was not measured).",
